# The two reduction-closure falsification witnesses refuse at seal under the
# exact local contract rules (`docs/spec/kernel.md` §4.1). A shape-only reading
# of either artifact would accept it: the transcript layout is untouched and
# only the exact local implication is broken.

# A check-free sumcheck reduction asserts the transition with no premises.
# RUN: sed 's/checks {final = "final", round1 = "round1", round2 = "round2"}/checks {}/' %S/../Encoding/sumcheck.mlir > %t.check-free.mlir
# RUN: not zkc-opt %pir-seal-full %t.check-free.mlir 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=CHECK-FREE %s
# CHECK-FREE: [zkc-E321] body-check roles do not exactly match reduction contract 'sumcheck'

# A KZG batch whose selected check carries an arbitrary suite is a different
# proposition than the one the contract pins.
# RUN: sed 's/params {suite = "bls12-381"}/params {suite = "toy-suite"}/' %S/../Encoding/kzg-after.mlir > %t.wrong-suite.mlir
# RUN: not zkc-opt %pir-seal-full %t.wrong-suite.mlir 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=WRONG-SUITE %s
# WRONG-SUITE: [zkc-E322] body role 'opening' has the wrong fixed parameters
